Subject: fade in after a seek in control mode

After a seek the converter is reset and the output starts in the middle of the
waveform, from silence to the value of the signal in one sample. The converter
overshoots on that step (0.5305 on a file that never goes above 0.5, after a
seek) and the step is a click. In control mode the output now fades in over the
first block after a seek, as it already did after a start or a pause. The
position and the way the player answers are unchanged.

Checked with three seeks during playback of a file that peaks at 0.5: the
highest level on the output was 0.502, it is 0.500 now.
--- a/cmd/rju-play.c
+++ b/cmd/rju-play.c
@@ -293,9 +293,12 @@ int signal_proc(jack_nframes_t nframes, void *PTR)
 			d->reader_frame_count = 0;
 			d->player_frame_count = 0;
 			d->ended = 0;
+			/* The output starts again from silence: it fades in, instead of
+			   starting in the middle of the waveform with a click. */
+			d->playing = 0;
 			d->play_pos = (double)s;
 			__atomic_store_n(&d->pub_pos, s, __ATOMIC_RELEASE);
-			__atomic_store_n(&d->pub_state, d->playing, __ATOMIC_RELEASE);
+			__atomic_store_n(&d->pub_state, __atomic_load_n(&d->ctl_play, __ATOMIC_ACQUIRE), __ATOMIC_RELEASE);
 			atomic_store_explicit(&d->o.seek_request, s, memory_order_release);
 		}
 	}
